# function found(k, look) { const map = new Map(); look(map); return map.get(k); }
# The call stands in tail position, so the read and the call are not one call of a stub: whatever is called leaves the frame behind, and an error of the call is worded at this site while the frame still stands.
# In front of the two stands a call of a stub that takes the receiver and the arguments: for a map as its class makes it the built-in answers, and the unit returns the answer.
# For every other receiver the stub has done nothing and answers the empty value, and the read and the tail call follow as they are written.
